@node Source Layout
@section Source Layout

Each utility is implemented in its own Zig source file at the top level of the
project, named after the utility (for example, @file{echo.zig} and
@file{stat.zig}).  The build is described by a single @file{build.zig}.  There
is no @file{build.zig.zon} manifest and there are no third-party packages.

Most source files begin with a copyright and SPDX license header:

@example
// Copyright (c) 2026 HiMitsu <himitsutha@@protonmail.com>
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
@end example

A few files in the current release (@file{base64.zig}, @file{date.zig},
@file{env.zig}, @file{stat.zig}, and @file{test.zig}) do not yet carry this
header.

@node Coding Conventions
@section Coding Conventions

@itemize @bullet
@item
Write clear, self-contained code: each utility has a single @code{main}
function and does not depend on other utilities in the project.
@item
Parse options explicitly and reject unsupported options with a clear message
rather than ignoring them.
@item
Prefer the Zig standard library for portable operations.  Use libc functions
only when the standard library does not provide the required behavior.
@item
Keep help text accurate.  Several utilities in the current release still carry
help text that describes behavior that is not implemented; for example,
@command{sleep} mentions time suffixes it does not accept, and
@command{seq} lists @option{-w} even though it is ignored.  Correcting such
text is a useful contribution.
@item
When you change a utility's behavior, update its section in
@file{docs/coreutils.texi} at the same time.
@end itemize

@node Adding a Utility
@section Adding a Utility

To add a new utility:

@enumerate
@item
Create a new file @file{@var{name}.zig} with a @code{main} function.
@item
Add the name to the @code{utils} array in @file{build.zig}.  The array is a
list of string literals; each entry is compiled from @file{@var{name}.zig}.
@item
Add a section to the appropriate chapter of this manual and an entry to the
overview table in @ref{Utilities Overview}.
@end enumerate

Do not rename or remove existing utilities without also updating
@file{build.zig} and this manual.

@node Testing
@section Testing

The repository does not currently contain an automated test suite, and
@file{build.zig} does not define a @code{test} step.  Contributions that add
tests are welcome.

To verify that the project builds, run:

@example
zig build
@end example

To check this manual for Texinfo errors, run:

@example
makeinfo --no-split -o /dev/null docs/coreutils.texi
@end example

